  <h2 id="parents">If you are a parent reading this chart</h2>

  <figure class="article-visual">
    <img src="/images/blog/career-options/career-chart-after-12th/career-chart-after-12th-decision-parent-reading-chart.webp" alt="Parent decision guide showing how to improve a child’s career choice through a near-term action, evidence-based placement reading, a plan B, and family-specific fit." title="If you are a parent reading this chart" width="1600" height="1000" loading="lazy" />
    <figcaption>Your role is to improve the quality of the decision, not to replace your child’s decision.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <p>
    Your role is to improve the quality of the decision, not to replace your child’s decision.
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li>Ask what your child can finish this month, not only which college name sounds safe.</li>
    <li>Read placement claims by median and by the number placed against the full batch.</li>
    <li>Agree on a plan B before results, so a bad paper does not become a family crisis.</li>
    <li>Do not judge a route by the neighbour’s child. Compare the route to your own family budget and your child’s energy.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    <a href="/blog/career-guidance/best-career-for-my-child-after-12th-india/">The best career for my child after 12th</a> and <a href="/blog/career-options/career-options-after-12th-for-girls-in-india/">career options after 12th for girls</a> go deeper on family conversations.
  </p>

